# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Added to dependencies in `package.json`
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependency tree

### 2. Analytics Integration
Modified `app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
- Placement follows Vercel's recommended practice for Next.js App Router

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- Identified this as a Next.js 16.2.12 project using the App Router pattern
- Located root layout at `app/layout.tsx`
- Followed the Next.js App Router specific installation instructions

### Code Integration
The Analytics component was strategically placed:
- After the theme initialization script
- After the main children content
- Before the closing body tag

This ensures analytics tracking is loaded after the main content while still being part of the root layout for all pages.

### Verification
- ✅ Linter passes with no errors on modified file
- ✅ TypeScript syntax is valid
- ✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality
- ✅ Package-lock.json properly updated

## Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project's Analytics tab
   - Click the "Enable" button
3. Analytics will begin tracking page views and web vitals automatically

## Notes
- The Analytics component requires no additional configuration for basic tracking
- All tracking is privacy-focused and GDPR-compliant by default
- Data collection only begins after deployment to Vercel with Analytics enabled in the dashboard
